Create a template for a formal letter including the organization name, contact information, date, and CC email field. Use CSS to add a border around the template and adjust the font size and color.

## Step 1: Create the basic HTML structure for the template
```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
<head>
	<title>Formal Letter Template</title>
	<style>
		/* Add a border around the template */
		.template {
			border: 1px solid #000;
			padding: 10px;
			width: 80%;
			margin: 20px auto;
		}

		/* Adjust the font size and color */
		.template h1 {
			font-size: 24px;
			color: #00698f;
		}

		.template p {
			font-size: 18px;
			color: #333;
		}
	</style>
</head>
<body>
	<div class="template">
		<h1>Formal Letter Template</h1>
		<p>
			Organization Name: <input type="text" id="organization" name="organization"><br>
			Contact Information: <input type="text" id="contact" name="contact"><br>
			Date: <input type="date" id="date" name="date"><br>
			To: <input type="text" id="to" name="to"><br>
			Subject: <input type="text" id="subject" name="subject"><br>
			CC: <input type="email" id="cc" name="cc"><br>
		</p>
	</div>
</body>
</html>
```

